From: Leopold Li <leopold.lixiaoliang@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 17:23:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] feat(gateway): queue ACK shows position number for
 message tracking
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Problem
-------
The queue-mode ACK "📥 Queued (排队中)" told the user their message was
received, but not WHICH message. With multiple follow-ups queued during
a busy turn, responses arriving out of visible order made it impossible
to map "which reply belongs to which input?".

Fix
---
Include the queue position in the ACK: "📥 Queued #{N} (排队中)" where N
is the slot this message will land in (current depth + 1, because
_handle_active_session_busy_message runs BEFORE the caller enqueues).

Position derived from GatewayRunner._queue_depth(session_key, adapter=..)
which sums the adapter head slot + runner overflow list. Wrapped in
try/except so a depth-lookup failure still delivers a bare "Queued" ACK
rather than nothing.

Example flow (user A busy, sends B and C during the turn):
  B arrives → ACK: "📥 Queued #1 (排队中)"
  C arrives within 30s → debounced, no ACK
  Main turn finishes → response for A
  Drain: B processed → response for B (user knows "#1" was B)
  Drain: C processed → response for C (user infers "next")

The 30s debounce still applies (interrupt/steer/queue share the window).
Rapid-burst ACK spam prevention wins over per-message identification
when user types 3+ follow-ups in quick succession.

Tests
-----
test_busy_text_mode_queue_sends_ack_by_default now asserts the ACK
matches r"Queued #\d+" — pins the position marker as a contract.
Full suite: 50/50 pass.

Backlog ref: agents/todo/backlog/2026-07-20_020_...ack-ux.md
---
 gateway/run.py                         | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 tests/gateway/test_busy_session_ack.py |  6 ++++++
 2 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gateway/run.py b/gateway/run.py
index b922584..43b99b6 100644
--- a/gateway/run.py
+++ b/gateway/run.py
@@ -5334,11 +5334,25 @@ class GatewayRunner(GatewayAuthorizationMixin, GatewayKanbanWatchersMixin, Gatew
             if not adapter:
                 return
 
+            # Position of THIS message in the queue: current depth counts
+            # everything already queued; this message hasn't been enqueued
+            # yet (the caller does that after _handle_active_session_busy_message
+            # returns False), so +1 gives the slot this message will land in.
+            try:
+                position = self._queue_depth(session_key, adapter=adapter) + 1
+            except Exception:
+                position = None
+
+            if position is not None:
+                content = f"📥 Queued #{position} (排队中)"
+            else:
+                content = "📥 Queued (排队中)"
+
             reply_anchor = self._reply_anchor_for_event(event)
             self._busy_ack_ts[session_key] = now
             await adapter._send_with_retry(
                 chat_id=event.source.chat_id,
-                content="📥 Queued (排队中)",
+                content=content,
                 reply_to=reply_anchor,
                 metadata=self._thread_metadata_for_source(event.source, reply_anchor),
             )
diff --git a/tests/gateway/test_busy_session_ack.py b/tests/gateway/test_busy_session_ack.py
index bb094c5..3c26657 100644
--- a/tests/gateway/test_busy_session_ack.py
+++ b/tests/gateway/test_busy_session_ack.py
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
 Verifies that users get an immediate status response instead of total silence
 when the agent is working on a task. See PR fix for the @Lonely__MH report.
 """
+import re
 import time
 from unittest.mock import AsyncMock, MagicMock, patch
 
@@ -275,6 +276,11 @@ class TestBusySessionAck:
         adapter._send_with_retry.assert_called_once()
         content = adapter._send_with_retry.call_args.kwargs.get("content", "")
         assert "Queued" in content, f"expected queue ACK marker, got: {content!r}"
+        # ACK identifies position of the queued message so the user can
+        # match subsequent responses back to their inputs.
+        assert re.search(r"Queued #\d+", content), (
+            f"expected position marker like 'Queued #N', got: {content!r}"
+        )
 
     @pytest.mark.asyncio
     async def test_busy_text_mode_queue_silent_when_ack_disabled(self, monkeypatch):
